--Purpose of the report:
--1. Present to business 5 attachements with the summary based on part types
--2. Part type to be determined based on the item number
--3. Reports are already pivoted (totals included), thus no need to train staff on Excel Pivots
--4. Reports run for a specific date range (typically yesterday 00:00 till yesterday 23:59)

--Assumptions:
--1. Max pallet qty is 24, although at places can be 12, 16, etc as well based on the item size
--2. Any lists for less than the qty against the item footprints for Pallet qty will be treated as less than a pallet
--3. Work assignment rules are configured to have break values equal to the pallet qty for the item number (normally at a part family level - XYZ part family has qty of 18 for Pallet UOM)

[select trunc(sysdate -6) run_from_date,
        trunc(sysdate) run_till_date,
        to_char(sysdate -6, 'dd.mm.yyyy') from_date,
        to_char(sysdate, 'dd.mm.yyyy') till_date
   from dual]
|
